<body>
    <h1>Logic+ Subroutine</h1>
    <div class=3D"Section1">
        <div class=3D"contentLayout2">
<div class=3D"columnLayout fixed-width" data-layout=3D"fixed-width">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<p>The =E2=80=9CLogic + Subroutine=E2=80=9D panel enables the execution of =
a selected Logic and returns its output to your flow, allowing one Logic to=
 run within another to complete a task seamlessly.</p>
<p>This panel can execute any Logic accessible in your company=E2=80=99s Sh=
arpen account, including those created by you or other users.</p><span clas=
s=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embed=
ded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" widt=
h=3D"387" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"ad445aca42cb5777ea300fe8d5a03c78216561ad2=
6ea23f4184edfd594a39baf" data-image-src=3D"https://sharpencx.atlassian.net/=
wiki/download/attachments/4236312577/Screenshot%202024-10-25%20at%202.22.04=
%E2%80%AFPM.png?version=3D2&amp;modificationDate=3D1729891354849&amp;cacheV=
ersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"113" data-width=3D"539" data-unreso=
lved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"4236017669" data-linked=
-resource-version=3D"2" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linke=
d-resource-default-alias=3D"Screenshot 2024-10-25 at 2.22.04=E2=80=AFPM.png=
" data-base-url=3D"https://sharpencx.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resour=
ce-content-type=3D"image/png" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"42363125=
77" data-linked-resource-container-version=3D"5" data-media-id=3D"4b88437e-=
1d22-477d-add0-3102ce85ead3" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"81"></span>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #EAE6FF;border-color: #998D=
D9;border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #EAE6FF;">
<p>The Logic+ Subroutine panel primary use case is to connect with external=
 platforms and pull in useful data as a flow within a flow. It=E2=80=99s no=
t designed for standard IVR tasks like transferring calls to queues or play=
ing prompts. Instead, it helps with things like doing data lookups, retriev=
ing information, and adding extra details to calls for various use cases.</=
p>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"Logic+Subroutine-Usingthispanel">Using this panel</h2>
<p>The Subroutine panel streamlines building and maintaining your Logics. B=
eing able to call an existing Logic to complete a task means not needing to=
 build a solution by hand every time. This panel allows you to create and u=
se Logics like reusable building blocks to enhance other Logic flows or ass=
emble more complex ones.</p>
<p>For example, you could create standalone Logics for common, core tasks=
=E2=80=94for example, returning a customer's account number based on input=
=E2=80=94and simply use the Subroutine panel to call them when needed withi=
n another Logic.</p>
<div class=3D"panel" style=3D"background-color: #C0B6F2;border-width: 1px;"=
>
<div class=3D"panelContent" style=3D"background-color: #C0B6F2;">
<p><strong>TIP: Test any target Logic on its own first.</strong><br>
The Subroutine panel does not check whether its targeted Logic actually wor=
ks as intended. You are responsible for testing a Logic first to ensure tha=
t it does work before selecting it with this panel.</p>
</div>
</div>
<h2 id=3D"Logic+Subroutine-Configuration">Configuration</h2>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"columnLayout two-equal" data-layout=3D"two-equal">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<p>The Subroutine panel has the following settings as shown in <strong>Figu=
re 2</strong>:</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Set as Flow Initiator</strong>: By selecting "Set as Flow Initia=
tor," this panel will serve as the starting point of the IVR flow, before p=
roceeding to subsequent panels within the Logic+ flow.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Panel Name</strong>: It is recommended that you choose a name an=
d keep it consistent. You will also need to specify the variable name to up=
date. If the variable does not exist, it will be created.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Panel Description</strong>: It is recommended to provide a clear=
 description of the panel, detailing its purpose and functionality. This is=
 akin to documentation, making it easier for others to understand and ident=
ify its intended use when they encounter it.</p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>LogicId</strong>: The Logic+ flow or mechanism that you would li=
ke to utilize with this panel.</p>
<ol start=3D"1">
<li>
<p><strong>Use Dropdown:</strong> Select an option from the dropdown menu.<=
/p></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Use Variable:</strong> Enter a variable. This field accepts eith=
er a unique ID string assigned to each Logic or a user-defined variable con=
taining such a string. <em>See the <strong>Logic+ ID</strong> section for d=
etails on finding a Logic=E2=80=99s ID.</em></p></li>
</ol></li>
<li>
<p><strong>Exit Paths:</strong> Use the dropdown menu to select another pan=
el in your flow. Any output from this panel will advance to the linked pane=
l.</p></li>
</ol>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper conflu=
ence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-ce=
nter" width=3D"354" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"052cde1f619ae718881a05c3417733f=
7d611d53185aef77d940afc76b1516cdd" data-image-src=3D"https://sharpencx.atla=
ssian.net/wiki/download/attachments/4236312577/Screenshot%202024-10-28%20at=
%2011.50.29%E2%80%AFAM-20241028-190634.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=
=3D1730142662010&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"658" dat=
a-width=3D"392" data-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=
=3D"4238409735" data-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-typ=
e=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"Screenshot 2024-10-2=
8 at 11.50.29=E2=80=AFAM-20241028-190634.png" data-base-url=3D"https://shar=
pencx.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" d=
ata-linked-resource-container-id=3D"4236312577" data-linked-resource-contai=
ner-version=3D"5" data-media-id=3D"0c215eee-ad92-4068-b6f4-bb774b101a45" da=
ta-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"593"></span>
<p><em> Figure 2: Configuring the Subroutine panel.</em></p>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"columnLayout fixed-width" data-layout=3D"fixed-width">
<div class=3D"cell normal" data-type=3D"normal">
<div class=3D"innerCell">
<h2 id=3D"Logic+Subroutine-Logic+ID:">Logic+ ID:</h2>
<ul>
<li>
<p><strong>Finding a Logic=E2=80=99s ID string.</strong> First, open the de=
sired Logic in the editor. From here, the current Logic=E2=80=99s ID can be=
 found in one place:</p>
<ul>
<li>
<p><em><strong>The URL bar:</strong></em> Look at the following section of =
the URL, as shown in <strong>Figure 3</strong>. Copy the ID string for late=
r use with the Subroutine panel.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul><span class=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper c=
onfluence-embedded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image ima=
ge-center" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"251d8a614642eb91d16730c25b=
3eab1185a574ed0e7e5287d83b4581c010a2d0" data-image-src=3D"https://sharpencx=
.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/4236312577/finding%20a%20logic%20I=
D.png?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1730143172168&amp;cacheVersion=3D1=
&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"29" data-width=3D"490" data-unresolved-commen=
t-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"4238344196" data-linked-resource-v=
ersion=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-=
default-alias=3D"finding a logic ID.png" data-base-url=3D"https://sharpencx=
.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/png" data-l=
inked-resource-container-id=3D"4236312577" data-linked-resource-container-v=
ersion=3D"5" data-media-id=3D"c9be309d-26a6-4dde-88fc-1593432f3f87" data-me=
dia-type=3D"file" height=3D"27"></span>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
    </div>
</body>
</html>
